  "title": "Canal Kitchen",
  "rules": [
    "Two kitchen banks share one timed footbridge and one four-tick cargo ferry. Three cooks can change roles freely.",
    "Left vegetables need two-tick chopping; right broth needs three-tick cooking. Both go into the right assembly tray.",
    "A clean bowl turns both prepared ingredients into a meal. Delivery returns that same bowl dirty.",
    "Only two bowls exist. Send them back to the left sink, wash for two ticks, and circulate them again.",
    "The bridge permits entry during the first four ticks of each eight-tick cycle. A cook on it can always leave.",
    "The ferry carries exactly one real item; it travels with food age and cannot be unloaded mid-channel.",
    "Cooked broth and meals spoil at age 12, while an unattended ready pot burns at age eight.",
    "Serve before each order deadline. Serving pays all cooks; unresolved deadlines cost the whole team.",
    "Use aproned characters, visible ingredients, bowls, steaming cookware and a wooden skiff on the actual canal geometry."
  ],
